# Repo-wide source rewrites require explicit approval

**Never run a repo-wide command that changes source code without Samuel explicitly asking for that command.**

This applies to every project, every plan, and every context — no exceptions.

## Commands that require a yes first

- `eslint --fix` on a directory or the whole repo, including `eslint --fix .` and `eslint --fix src/`
- `prettier --write`, `prettier --format`, or any Prettier invocation that rewrites files across a tree
- `npm run lint` or any other script when that script itself runs a fixer such as `eslint --fix`
- Codemods, `sed`/`perl` rewrites, or formatters applied across many files

## What to do instead

- Edit the specific files the task requires.
- Run linters and formatters in check-only mode (`eslint`, `prettier --check`) and report the results.
- If a fixer would clean things up, stop and ask before running it. Name the command and which files it would change.

## What counts as a violation

- Running `eslint --fix` or Prettier write/format to make a new config pass.
- "Fixing" a batch of lint or format findings by rewriting the tree.
- Hiding a fixer inside a larger install, typecheck, or lint step.
